Sval: the check for the default browser at launch stays open while Sval is it

Settings' "Always check if Sval is your default browser" sets
browser.shell.checkDefaultBrowser, which DefaultBrowserCheck reads at each
launch: it asks only when Sval is not the default. Firefox disables the
checkbox while Firefox is the default, so a user cannot ask to be told if
another browser takes the default later. The setting's disabled callback is
built in Firefox's main.js, so no added file can change it.

diff --git a/browser/components/preferences/main.js b/browser/components/preferences/main.js
index 29d3f08fb7..fbdbaed8a6 100644
--- a/browser/components/preferences/main.js
+++ b/browser/components/preferences/main.js
@@ -534,10 +534,9 @@ Preferences.addSetting({
    * browser is already the default browser.
    */
   visible: () => DefaultBrowserHelper.canCheck,
-  disabled: (_, setting) =>
-    !DefaultBrowserHelper.canCheck ||
-    setting.locked ||
-    DefaultBrowserHelper.isBrowserDefault,
+  // Sval: the check stays open while Sval is the default, so a user can ask
+  // to be told at launch if another browser takes the default later.
+  disabled: (_, setting) => !DefaultBrowserHelper.canCheck || setting.locked,
 });
 
 Preferences.addSetting({
